## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates design of a scalable, non-destructive editing pipeline, leveraging Swift concurrency, Core Image, and memory-aware rendering. Also tests undo/redo, testability, and accessibility considerations in a production-like feature.

## Key Concepts
- Swift concurrency and actors for safe state sharing
- Core Image for GPU-accelerated filters
- Non-destructive editing via composable filter passes
- Undo/redo through graph state snapshots
- Memory management with tile-based rendering and lazy recomputation
- Testability: unit tests for graph evaluation; integration tests for export
- Accessibility hooks for UI feedback

## Code Example
```swift
// Skeleton: Filter protocol and graph actor
actor FilterGraph {
  struct Node { var id: String; var filter: CIFilter }
  var nodes: [Node] = []
  func applyAll(base: CIImage) async -> CIImage {
    var current = base
    for n in nodes {
      n.filter.setValue(current, forKey: kCIInputImageKey)
      if let out = n.filter.outputImage {
        current = out
      }
    }
    return current
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this to handle very large images on memory-constrained devices?
- What trade-offs exist between tile-based rendering vs full-image compositing, and how would you test them?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses offline-first design, delta-based syncing, and conflict handling under intermittent connectivity, which are critical in collaboration apps used by teams.

## Key Concepts

- Core Data data model for Comment and Patch objects
- Delta/patch format including baseVersion, changes, and timestamps
- Reconciliation strategy (latest-writer-wins or server-validated merges)
- Robust test plan for offline edits, re-connect, and concurrency

## Code Example

```javascript
// Swift-like pseudocode: apply a patch to a Comment
func apply(patch: Patch, to comment: inout Comment) {
    // Validate base version matches current state
    guard patch.baseVersion == comment.version else {
        // Handle conflict resolution
        resolveConflict(patch: patch, comment: &comment)
        return
    }

    // Apply delta changes
    for change in patch.changes {
        switch change.type {
        case .insert:
            comment.text.insert(change.text, at: change.position)
        case .delete:
            comment.text.removeSubrange(change.range)
        case .replace:
            comment.text.replaceSubrange(change.range, with: change.text)
        }
    }

    // Update version and timestamps
    comment.version += 1
    comment.updatedAt = Date()
}
```

